@startuml cancel-shutdown-sequence
title M3b stop request, native join and Host-owned disposal
actor User
participant Host
participant InspectionEngine as Engine
participant InspectionRunner as Runner
participant NativeInspector as Inspector
participant "Native DLL / worker" as DLL
participant "Progress observer" as Observer
Runner -> Inspector : InspectAsync(job, samples, token)
Inspector -> Inspector : copy input / retain handle / root callback context
Inspector -> DLL : Start(samples, callback, context)
DLL --> Inspector : copied / started
Inspector -> DLL : Wait (dedicated waiter)
DLL -> Observer : callback through managed trampoline
User -> Engine : CancelRun(runId)
Engine -> Engine : first reason wins lock / CancelRequested
Engine ->> Inspector : token callback dispatch -> RequestStop
Inspector -> DLL : RequestStop (does not wait)
DLL --> Inspector : stop requested (or stop error)
Engine --> User : Accepted (still Busy)
Observer --> DLL : callback returns
DLL -> Inspector : possible late progress
Inspector --> DLL : suppress observer delivery after stop
alt Wait succeeds
DLL --> Inspector : worker joined / operation status + result
Inspector -> Inspector : unregister token / release context and extra handle reference
Inspector --> Runner : canceled, or termination error if stop failed
else Wait fails (termination unconfirmed)
DLL --> Inspector : Wait error
Inspector -> Inspector : retain context and handle reference until process exit
Inspector --> Runner : termination error (confirmed=false)
end
Runner --> Engine : runner error
Engine -> Engine : close arbitration / await token callbacks / dispose timer and CTS
Engine -> Engine : Canceled or TimedOut; termination error overrides as Faulted
Engine --> Host : completed snapshot (includes TerminationConfirmed)
Host -> Engine : await DisposeAsync()
Engine --> Host : Disposed, or remain Faulted
Host -> Inspector : await DisposeAsync()
opt termination confirmed
Inspector -> DLL : Destroy via SafeHandle
end
note over Host, Engine
Host shutdown closes admission and requests Shutdown before waiting.
Persistence already entered must finish saving.
Termination failure permanently blocks admission.
Unconfirmed Wait completion means managed failure arbitration, not native termination.
end note
@enduml
